<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Nina Simone, Pastel Blues</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Georgia Lee</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover, possibly the first Australian performance; banned from radio</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Siouxsie and the Banshees, Through the Looking Glass</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1987</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Jeff Buckley</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover, after hearing Siouxsie and the Banshees' version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Blood on the Leaves, Kanye West (Ye)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2013</span><span class="sg-chain-h">samples Nina Simone's recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Strange Fruit: The Biography of a Song, David Margolick</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2001</span><span class="sg-chain-h">book about the song</span></li></ul></section>
